direction: down
title: "C23 native node binding and caller authority"
"Native cache /800-object allocation" -> "Stable storage keys": "allocation/incarnation plus slot; no NodeId-to-address arithmetic"
"Raw list publication" -> "Owner initialization": "actual source order; incomplete publication is not complete binding"
"Stable storage keys" -> "Qualified binding view": "owner ready, live spans, injective mapping and field containment"
"Qualified binding view" -> "Reader closure seal": "direct census plus callbacks/instrumentation/platform scope"
"Reader closure seal" -> "Native target handoff": "payload leases settled; old target read authority closes"
"Native target handoff" -> "Allocated object role": "node storage incarnation unchanged; union role changes"
"Unknown handoff" -> "Stable source owner": "retain cache and return-domain duty; consumer progress is not source completion"
"Source completion" -> "Close metadata admission": "existing leases drain; native cleanup has independent receipt"
"Close metadata admission" -> "Fresh cache incarnation": "same address can be reused; old query key rejected"
"Fresh cache incarnation" -> "Opaque record lookup": "record service can answer without touching old/new native cache"
